  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure builds east across the Ohio Valley through Friday.\nDry conditions are expected to continue through the end of the\nweek with cooler than average conditions under broad northerly\nflow. Patchy fog remains possible across inland locations along\nand east of I-71. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nUnsettled weather returns this weekend as an upper level trough\nand associated surface low push into the Great Lakes region.\nShower and thunderstorm chances increase from west to east\novernight Friday into Saturday. There remains some disagreement \nacross models on the placement and trajectory of the weak \nsurface low and closed mid-level low which will ultimately \ndetermine coverage and timing of showers and storms, \nparticularly on Saturday. By Sunday, the upper trough glides \neast across the local area allowing for rain chances to \ngradually diminish from west to east through Sunday evening. \nGenerally anticipate coverage to remain isolated to scattered \nduring periods of showers and thunderstorms this weekend. Any \nshowers and storms that occur will be capable of producing heavy\nrain as PWAT values rise to 1.75-2.00 inches Saturday into \nSunday.",
